      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "<a id=\"_Toc492473451\">H 14770</a> – Abaan, from Ibn Abu Ya’four who said:",
          "<span class=\"first-chapter-phrase\"><span class=\"first-in-chapter character-a\">A</span>bu Abdullah</span><sup>asws</sup> said: ‘The one of adulterous birth should (also) perform deeds. If his deeds are good he would be Recompensated for it, and if his deeds are evil he would be Recompensed for it’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "323. Abaan, from Ibn Abu Ya’four who said: Abu Abdullah (a.s.) said: ‘The one of adulterous birth should (also) perform deeds. If his deeds are good he would be Recompensated for it, and if his deeds are evil he would be Recompensed for it’."
        ]
